sequenceDiagram
    participant old as busd that stops
    participant systemd
    systemd->>old: SIGTERM
    Note over old: pauses its clients, and<br/>hands their connections over
    old->>systemd: FDSTORE busd-state (the state memfd)
    old->>systemd: FDSTORE busd-clients (each queue socket)
    old->>systemd: BARRIER
    destroy old
    old->>systemd: exits
    Note over systemd: keeps the listening socket open, which<br/>queues the clients that connect
    create participant new as busd that starts
    systemd->>new: starts it with the passed FDs
    Note over new: raises its soft limit of<br/>open FDs to the hard one
    new->>systemd: FDSTOREREMOVE (each name)
    Note over new: reads the state memfd, and takes the<br/>connection FDs out of the queue sockets
    Note over new: restores the connections
    new->>systemd: READY=1
